WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.736
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.039
Thank you for being here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.207
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:10.676
Well, guys, it is Friday,
and it's pretty much

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:12.912
felt like that
since noon on Wednesday.

00:00:12.912 --> 00:00:15.514
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.514 --> 00:00:17.249
Yeah, today, my Apple Watch
was like,

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:18.751
"Your heart rate
hasn't hit 200 lately.

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:21.421
Are you okay?"

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.356
What a difference
a few days can make, though.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:26.492
Check out what the breaking news
was on CNN this morning.

00:00:26.492 --> 00:00:28.061 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:31.397 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]

00:00:31.397 --> 00:00:34.400 line:0%
-Yeah, well, today

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.836
was President Biden's
second full day in office,

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.838
and he spent it trying
to fix the economy.

00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:41.207
This afternoon, he signed
two executive orders

00:00:41.207 --> 00:00:43.776
meant to provide fast
economic relief.

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:46.045
Yep, Biden's taking on
America's biggest problems.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.615
Yesterday, it was the pandemic.
Today, it was the economy.

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.949
Tomorrow, it's people
who don't know

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.018
the Bernie Sanders
meme is over.

00:00:57.257 --> 00:01:00.492
"Put them in my back --"
Yeah, you missed it, man.

00:01:00.492 --> 00:01:02.595
Some more news
out of Washington this morning.

00:01:02.595 --> 00:01:04.497
Chuck Schumer spoke on
the Senate floor

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:06.699
about the impeachment
against Donald Trump,

00:01:06.699 --> 00:01:08.300
but he had a bit of a flub.

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:09.335
Listen to this.

00:01:09.335 --> 00:01:11.837 line:0%
-Senators will have to decide

00:01:11.837 --> 00:01:16.242 line:0%
if they believe Donald John --
Donald John Trump incited

00:01:16.242 --> 00:01:21.013 line:0%
the erection -- insurrection
against the United States.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:25.751
♪♪

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:31.624
-Well, someone's excited
to be Senate majority leader.

00:01:31.624 --> 00:01:34.493
I wasn't sure how the Democrats
planned to unify the country,

00:01:34.493 --> 00:01:36.562
but if it's with bloopers
like this, count me in.

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:38.230
I'm in.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:40.065
Meanwhile, down in Florida,
Disney World

00:01:40.065 --> 00:01:42.268
is making some updates since
there's now a new president.

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.402
Check it out.

00:01:43.402 --> 00:01:45.237 line:0%
-The Hall of Presidents
in Disney World

00:01:45.237 --> 00:01:47.306 line:0%
is closed
so technicians can add

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:50.342 line:0%
an animatronic version
of President Joe Biden.

00:01:50.342 --> 00:01:51.911
-And to keep it authentic,

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:54.280
the Biden robot will commute
every day on the monorail

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.915
from Delaware.

00:01:58.484 --> 00:02:00.352
Let me just say, you can add
any president you want,

00:02:00.352 --> 00:02:01.988
but the only robot
the kids are there to see

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.257
is William Howard Taft.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.394
Yep, a President Biden robot,

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.629
which means everyone in the hall
will be listening like...

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:13.532
-Corn Pop was a bad dude.

00:02:13.532 --> 00:02:16.436
And he ran a bunch of bad boys.

00:02:16.436 --> 00:02:18.838
And I did --
And back in those days,

00:02:18.838 --> 00:02:20.572
to show how things have changed,

00:02:20.572 --> 00:02:22.074
one of the things
you had to use,

00:02:22.074 --> 00:02:25.010
if you use pomade in your hair,
you had to wear a bathing cap.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:28.615
-Okay, I'm going to go grab
Mickey ears or something.

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:30.483
You kids know
where we're staying, right?

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:31.583
You remember where
we're staying?

00:02:31.583 --> 00:02:35.354
Good. Alright, I'm gonna leave.

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:36.990
You can make
your way back, right?

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.825
Okay.

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:42.561
"Corn Pop knew some bad dudes."

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.497
[ Laughs ]

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:45.664
-Dungarees.

00:02:45.664 --> 00:02:47.900
-He knew people like
Count Chocula

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:50.002
and stuff like that.

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:51.470
Some entertainment news
was just announced,

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:54.373
that the release date
for the new James Bond movie,

00:02:54.373 --> 00:02:58.878
"No Time to Die," has been
pushed back for a third time.

00:02:58.878 --> 00:03:00.580
At this point,
they've delayed it so long,

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.481
the technology
is going to look ridiculous.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:04.584
Like, "Mr. Bond,
your latest gadget

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:08.054
is a phone that takes pictures."

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.592
Yep, the film
has been delayed so much,

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:14.761
they've even had to update
the title a few times.

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:16.996
First, it was...

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.264 line:0%
Then it was...

00:03:20.332 --> 00:03:22.035 line:0%
And now it's like...

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:28.408 line:0%
"And then I'll
take it from there, and..."

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.743
Some business news.

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.979
Since the pandemic
has made travel difficult,

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:35.281
one airline has figured out
a new way to make money.

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:36.649
Watch this.

00:03:36.649 --> 00:03:39.952 line:0%
You can now get wine delivered
from American Airlines.

00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:42.588 line:0%
That airline has so much
leftover wine

00:03:42.588 --> 00:03:45.024 line:0%
that they're launching a new
wine-delivery subscription

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:46.726 line:0%
for $99 a month.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:49.962
-Yeah, not only that, they're
also selling the hummus pucks

00:03:49.962 --> 00:03:53.265
that were
stuffed between the seats.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:54.733
Who wants a puck?
Who wants a puck?

00:03:54.733 --> 00:03:56.335
Come on.

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:58.171 line:0%
And, finally, I saw
that Dunkin' Donuts

00:03:58.171 --> 00:04:02.575 line:0%
is now adding salads to its menu
at select locations.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.944 line:0%
Yeah, when you order a salad
from Dunkin' Donuts,

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:06.645 line:0%
even the workers are like,
"No, seriously,

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:08.180 line:0%
what can I get you?"

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.916
We have a great show tonight.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:11.684
Give it up for The Roots,
everybody!

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:14.386
-♪ Paragraphs slash
your phonograph in half ♪

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:16.823
♪ It be the legendary
back on a warpath ♪

00:04:16.823 --> 00:04:18.891
♪ First class,
leaving mics in a cast ♪

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:23.930
♪ Causing ruckus like
the aftermath when it blast ♪

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:26.098
-What a show
we have for you tonight.

00:04:26.098 --> 00:04:30.469
You can see her as a judge
on "Go-Big Show" on TBS.

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.371
Rosario Dawson is here.

00:04:32.371 --> 00:04:34.907
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:37.677
Maybe, maybe a little
Cory Booker cameo.

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:39.712
Just saying. Senator Booker.

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:43.248
Plus, he stars in the
TNT series "Snowpiercer."

00:04:43.248 --> 00:04:45.784
Daveed Diggs is here!

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:47.053
And we've got great music

00:04:47.053 --> 00:04:50.723
from Amanda Shires
featuring Jason Isbell.

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:54.860
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.896
Hey, man.
-Hey.

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.164
-Good to see you.
-Yeah.

00:04:59.164 --> 00:05:00.933
-Wow. You look good.

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.802
Did you get --
You look different.

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:05.071
-I took your advice.
-Is that right?

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:08.074
-Yeah. Last night,
I showed you the tattoo.

00:05:08.074 --> 00:05:12.812
You said, "Hey, you got to get
the other side done," so...

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:16.082
-The camera -- Check out...

00:05:16.082 --> 00:05:18.785
So...

00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:21.720
Was it...

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.656
Well, you look upset.
Was it --

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.525
-Well, I told
you I was having --

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:27.493
feeling a little buyer's remorse

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:29.429
and you said,
"No, no, it's your Lamborghini.

00:05:29.429 --> 00:05:30.430
You got to get
the other side done."

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.697
-Yeah.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:33.599
-So, you know, and I
was having second thoughts.

00:05:33.599 --> 00:05:35.234
Now I'm having third thoughts.

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:43.376
-I think it's good, man.
You got two tattoo.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.409
-Yeah.

00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:47.813
-Two tattoo.
-Tattoo part deux.

00:05:47.813 --> 00:05:49.248
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.918
-Look, you know what I say?

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:54.086
Two tat. Two tat.
Two, two, tat-tat-tat.

00:05:54.086 --> 00:05:56.255
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:57.823
[ Cymbal crash ]

00:05:57.823 --> 00:05:59.725
Oh, man. Oh, my God.

00:05:59.725 --> 00:06:02.695
Well, hey, if you don't
come Monday with a full...

00:06:02.695 --> 00:06:04.130
-Yeah.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:06.365
-I want, like, a crab on your
head or something like that.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:08.767
With a crab,
like two claws coming down.

00:06:08.767 --> 00:06:10.469
-You really think?
-Get sponsored -- Yeah, man.

00:06:10.469 --> 00:06:12.104
Get sponsored by --

00:06:12.104 --> 00:06:14.206
-See? I mean, because
I always felt like --

00:06:14.206 --> 00:06:16.275
I don't know -- like 45

00:06:16.275 --> 00:06:19.712
is probably the cutoff for
new face tattoos.

00:06:19.712 --> 00:06:21.647
-Absolutely not.
No, there's no cutoff.

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:22.715
No, no.
That's the time to get it.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:23.883
-Okay.

00:06:23.883 --> 00:06:25.451
-Because that's the time,
I think, where your skin

00:06:25.451 --> 00:06:29.922
kind of -- It's kind of
settled in already.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:32.458
I do want to bring
up something, by the way.

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:34.359
This is cool
that we get to do the show.

00:06:34.359 --> 00:06:35.528
Obviously, we're very lucky
to do this.

00:06:35.528 --> 00:06:38.597
But we have
the best band in the world

00:06:38.597 --> 00:06:39.765
with Tariq and The Roots.

00:06:39.765 --> 00:06:42.301
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:44.737
But Kirk,
Captain Kirk Douglas,

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:46.372
on guitar, who's one of
the greatest

00:06:46.372 --> 00:06:51.978
guitarists in the world,
has his own signature Gibson SG.

00:06:51.978 --> 00:06:53.112
Look at this.
-Whoo!

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:55.715
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:06:55.715 --> 00:06:57.516
-Yes!

00:06:57.516 --> 00:07:00.119
-Kirk, talk to me about this.
It just came out.

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:01.520
I'm excited about this.
-Thank you.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:06.225
Yeah, it just came out this past
Wednesday, and this is it.

00:07:06.225 --> 00:07:09.194
This is in Inverness Green.

00:07:09.194 --> 00:07:10.496
-What did you put --

00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:12.131
What are the specs
that you did, that you put in?

00:07:12.131 --> 00:07:14.199
-Well, one of the things --
I don't know if you remember,

00:07:14.199 --> 00:07:15.801
but a while back,

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:18.003
there was this artist
that was on the show, Prince,

00:07:18.003 --> 00:07:22.441
and he broke a guitar that was
very near and dear to me.

00:07:22.441 --> 00:07:24.343
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:26.812
So, that guitar
is actually in Cleveland,

00:07:26.812 --> 00:07:28.681
at the Rock &amp; Roll Hall of Fame.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:29.915
-Is it really?

00:07:29.915 --> 00:07:33.018
-Yeah, it is right now.
And I missed that guitar.

00:07:33.018 --> 00:07:35.188
So when Gibson came to me
and they wanted to do

00:07:35.188 --> 00:07:37.423
a signature guitar with me,

00:07:37.423 --> 00:07:38.591
before I sent it down there,

00:07:38.591 --> 00:07:42.261
I sent the
broken Prince guitar to Gibson,

00:07:42.261 --> 00:07:45.064
and they replicated the specs
of that neck.

00:07:45.064 --> 00:07:48.100
So while that guitar
is in Cleveland,

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.435
I have this guitar,

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:52.405
and when I feel this neck
of this signature guitar,

00:07:52.405 --> 00:07:56.709
I feel the neck of the broken...

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:57.776
Yeah.

00:07:57.776 --> 00:08:00.012
-The Captain Kirk Douglas SG.

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:02.048
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:03.549
-I'm so proud of you.
I love the color.

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:05.284
-Thank you, man.
-That's awesome, bud.

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:09.622
Hey, so,
during the quarantine,

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:11.657
you know, we were doing
the show from --

00:08:11.657 --> 00:08:13.292
I was doing the show
from my house

00:08:13.292 --> 00:08:15.261
and just staying in there.

00:08:15.261 --> 00:08:17.963
And when they
finally, like, let --

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:20.299
They opened up essential
businesses and stuff like that,

00:08:20.299 --> 00:08:23.936
I went to a hardware store
to get a light switch.

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.805
I was going to install
a light switch.

00:08:25.805 --> 00:08:28.741
-[ Laughs ]
-Yeah, I did.

00:08:28.741 --> 00:08:30.342
And I did a good job.
-Okay.

00:08:30.342 --> 00:08:33.145
-I know how to do it.
So, I go to this hardware store.

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:36.649
So, I'm in the hardware store
and I hear this song playing.

00:08:36.649 --> 00:08:38.250
And it's so good.
I go, "What is that song?

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.685
Do I know this one?
And it was like...

00:08:39.685 --> 00:08:41.787
♪ If you're gonna go down ♪

00:08:41.787 --> 00:08:44.022
♪ I'm gonna go down swingin' ♪

00:08:44.022 --> 00:08:47.593
And I go, "Oh, that's great."
So I Shazam the song.

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:50.729
I go -- And it's by
Thad Cockrell.

00:08:50.729 --> 00:08:52.565
T-H-A-D Cockrell.

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:54.266
And it's about, like --

00:08:54.266 --> 00:08:57.836
Anyways, it's about, like,
if I lost you...

00:08:57.836 --> 00:09:00.506
Let me just play a little jam
of it here, 'cause it's good.

00:09:00.506 --> 00:09:03.175
So, it's probably --
It's almost like two songs.

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:04.309
It's this jam. It's like...

00:09:04.309 --> 00:09:05.811
-♪ ...I would do ♪

00:09:05.811 --> 00:09:07.746
♪ If all we lost ♪

00:09:07.746 --> 00:09:09.014
♪ If I lost you ♪

00:09:09.014 --> 00:09:11.317
-So, "If I lost you," right?
And then it goes...

00:09:11.317 --> 00:09:13.919
-♪ If I'm gonna go down ♪

00:09:13.919 --> 00:09:17.489
♪ I want to go down swinging ♪

00:09:17.489 --> 00:09:20.892
-So, I didn't
rock out like that,

00:09:20.892 --> 00:09:23.729
but in my head -- I had the mask
on and everything,

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:26.064
and I'm just like, "Oh, this is
the jam right there, man."

00:09:26.064 --> 00:09:27.132
So, I was maybe doing
a little of this groove

00:09:27.132 --> 00:09:28.333
type of thing.

00:09:28.333 --> 00:09:30.436
But then it became my anthem,
because I'm like,

00:09:30.436 --> 00:09:31.570
"Yeah, man, this is, like --"

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:33.205
When you want
to give up, don't give up.

00:09:33.205 --> 00:09:36.041
Just -- If you're going to go
down, you go down swinging, man.

00:09:36.041 --> 00:09:37.576
-Yeah.
-So, I get into it.

00:09:37.576 --> 00:09:39.911
This is my anthem.
I love the song.

00:09:39.911 --> 00:09:42.615
Anyways, long story long.

00:09:42.615 --> 00:09:45.917
Thad Cockrell --
he released this record.

00:09:45.917 --> 00:09:47.753
No one knows
there's gonna be a pandemic.

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:49.955
They put all this work into
this album, and it comes out.

00:09:49.955 --> 00:09:50.989
They have a pandemic.

00:09:50.989 --> 00:09:53.759
Your whole plan's
pushed to the side.

00:09:53.759 --> 00:09:55.794
So, if you go
on his Instagram,

00:09:55.794 --> 00:09:58.430
he tells this story,
and it moved me.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:02.367
Anyways, so, he writes a
whole manifesto to his manager

00:10:02.367 --> 00:10:06.204
and says, "I got to think of
something else to do.

00:10:06.204 --> 00:10:10.076
I think I'm going to stop.
I'll think of a different job.

00:10:10.076 --> 00:10:12.545
I mean, I have
other things I can do.

00:10:12.545 --> 00:10:13.912
I'm talented.
I could do something else."

00:10:13.912 --> 00:10:18.050
So he's actually going to
to start something new.

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.286
And on January 3rd,
he sends it to his manager.

00:10:21.286 --> 00:10:25.490
January 4th, the manager
calls him, and they they said,

00:10:25.490 --> 00:10:27.626
"We're not going to talk about
this manifesto thing,

00:10:27.626 --> 00:10:31.430
because we just got a phone call
from 'The Tonight Show.'"

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.432
And, yeah, he's
like, "You're going to be on

00:10:33.432 --> 00:10:34.499
'The Tonight Show.'"

00:10:34.499 --> 00:10:35.601
And he was like, "What?"

00:10:35.601 --> 00:10:38.804
And he said that he cried
for an hour.

00:10:38.804 --> 00:10:40.338
They thought the phone cut out.

00:10:40.338 --> 00:10:41.874
He's like,
"Did the phone cut out?"

00:10:41.874 --> 00:10:43.308
He's like, "It's just like --"

00:10:43.308 --> 00:10:44.577
And he goes,
"It just goes to show,

00:10:44.577 --> 00:10:46.778
don't give up,
because you never know if

00:10:46.778 --> 00:10:51.349
Some moron is going to walk into
a hardware store

00:10:51.349 --> 00:10:53.986
and Shazam your song."

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:58.857
And he is coming on our show
Tuesday, this Tuesday.

00:10:58.857 --> 00:11:00.058
Thad Cockrell.

